            <ArticleTitle>Management of chronic osteoarthritic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>933-49, ix</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoarthritis is a common cause of chronic pain in small animals. Although there is currently no known cure, the disease can often be palliated by a combination of weight control, regulated exercise, anti-inflammatory medications, and disease-modifying osteoarthritic agents. The diagnosis, recommended treatments, and many of the newer drugs and disease-modifying agents are discussed in this article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
